`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Paper-described interface."})," A selector receives a visual rubric, executed input trace with render timestamps, and observation budget. It requests replay positions/intervals; a deterministic resolver returns recorded frames. The final judge receives frames and rubric, producing item scores, rationales and cited frame IDs. In its matched-budget experiment, requests resolve to the first captured frame at or after the requested timestamp, subsequent requests can use observed frames, and every inspected frame counts toward the budget."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Reported finding and qualification."})," Across 244 replays from 50 generated Small games, adaptive selection won 60.5% of the 1,159 preference-bearing item comparisons. Among all 4,102 comparisons, 17.1% favored adaptive, 11.2% uniform, 69.4% were equivalent and 2.3% insufficient. This is model-audited rationale support, not correctness against reference labels. Method names were masked but paths retained source-directory names. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2609.39564v1",children:"Paper v1, §§D.2 and G.3"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Availability and terms."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/krafton-ai/a2z-gamespec-bench",children:"official repository"})," explicitly says code is forthcoming; its inspected tree has documentation/assets rather than a released evaluator. Do not repeat the abstract’s broader availability claim as proof of an executable selector. Original repository code/GDDs/contracts are MIT, third-party materials retain their own terms. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/datasets/KRAFTON/A2Z-GameSpec-Bench",children:"dataset card"})," releases 100 GDD/contract/scenario tasks, all in ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"test"}),"; Small/Big are size categories, not train/test partitions. It specifies Phaser 4.1, TypeScript and Vite."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap adaptation, unimplemented."})," Use this first for brief UI feedback and action-triggered transitions. Baseline: uniformly spaced original-resolution frames from the ",e.jsx(t.em,{children:"same recording"}),". Candidate: trace-guided frames, matched by total inspected pixels/frames, including exploratory retrievals. Measure annotated transition coverage and unsupported verdicts. Input events are not proof of rendered outcomes. Keep evaluator-only requirements out of agent context."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"2-v--seal-guided-crops-plus-visual-working-memory",children:"2. V* / SEAL: guided crops plus visual working memory"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Mechanism."})," The VQA model names missing target objects, searches, and reasons over the question, global image, crops and locations. Working memory is per-question context. On 191 V*Bench examples, the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.14135v2",children:"v2 paper, Table 2 and §5.2"})," reports 75.39% for SEAL versus 45.02% for a no-memory/search LLaVA-style model trained on the same data. This is not merely switching search off in a frozen checkpoint. Keeping working memory but substituting GroundingDINO or OWL-ViT gives 62.30% or 62.82%, a closer comparison of search against direct detection. These are specialized high-resolution image-QA results, not game-editor or repair gains."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Source-inspected interface."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/penghao-wu/vstar/blob/4ede6647959cfb59eeabd09286adf6a5f9478da0/visual_search.py",children:e.jsx(t.code,{children:"visual_search.py"})})," accepts a PIL image, target-object text, search model, minimum patch size, confidence thresholds and optional visualization target box. It returns ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"(final_step, path_length, search_successful, all_valid_boxes)"}),". The search recursively divides patches, prioritizes target/context heatmaps, and can fall back to a lower-confidence candidate. A final-step detection is crop-local pixel ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"(x,y,w,h)"}),"; the enclosing patch has its own original-image offset. The success flag is therefore mandatory evidence, not redundant metadata. In the no-candidate path, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"final_step"})," can remain ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"None"})," before being dereferenced: this is a source-visible edge case, not a reproduced crash."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/penghao-wu/vstar/blob/4ede6647959cfb59eeabd09286adf6a5f9478da0/app.py",children:e.jsx(t.code,{children:"app.py"})})," adds crop offsets, extracts slightly expanded object crops (",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"patch_scale=1.2"}),"), then maps boxes through square-image padding and normalization before the final VQA call. The demo warns that its search focuses on common objects and single-instance cases."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Availability and terms."})," Public code, benchmark and checkpoint links appear in the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/penghao-wu/vstar",children:"README"}),". Repository ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/penghao-wu/vstar/blob/main/LICENSE",children:"LICENSE"})," is MIT. The linked ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/craigwu/seal_vqa_7b",children:"VQA"})," and ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/craigwu/seal_vsm_7b",children:"search-model"})," pages had no substantive model card or license declaration in the inspected page; code MIT is not a clearance for weights, base model or images."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap adaptation, unimplemented."})," Compare global screenshot only, fixed grid crops, and query-directed crops at matched image/token budgets. Keep the global screenshot so local crops do not erase spatial context. Each crop needs source frame hash, pixel box, transform and explicit search-success status. Add absent-target and repeated-instance cases; do not translate failed search into proof an object is absent."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"3-videotree-relevance-dependent-breadth-and-depth",children:"3. VideoTree: relevance-dependent breadth and depth"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Source-inspected interface."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Ziyang412/VideoTree/blob/605ec8e917f9a0f95d37a73a0b50bf0e8cfe076e/adaptive_breath_expansion.py",children:e.jsx(t.code,{children:"adaptive_breath_expansion.py"})})," consumes per-video ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:".pt"})," frame features and question/caption records. It clusters feature vectors, chooses representative frame offsets, obtains relevance scores, and writes per-video predictions plus ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"width_res.json"})," containing ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"name"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"tree_node"}),", and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"cluster_ids_x"}),". It doubles breadth until enough scores equal 3 or the maximum is reached; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Ziyang412/VideoTree/blob/main/util.py",children:e.jsx(t.code,{children:"defaults"})})," are breadth 8→32 and four highly relevant frames."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Ziyang412/VideoTree/blob/605ec8e917f9a0f95d37a73a0b50bf0e8cfe076e/depth_expansion.py",children:e.jsx(t.code,{children:"depth_expansion.py"})})," consumes those cluster assignments, features and relevance scores. Score 1 retains a representative; score 2 expands one level; score 3 expands two. It exports ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"name"}),", time-sorted ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"sorted_values"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"relevance"}),". Paths are hard-coded placeholders."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Important representation boundary."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Ziyang412/VideoTree/blob/605ec8e917f9a0f95d37a73a0b50bf0e8cfe076e/prompts.py",children:e.jsx(t.code,{children:"prompts.py"})})," selects captions for the final prompt, not original frame pixels. Audit index conventions before reuse: representative tensor offsets are zero-based, while the caption-selection code keeps positive offsets and uses ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"captions[i-1]"}),". This source-level mapping concern requires a fixture, not a runtime-defect claim."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Reported finding."})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.19209v2",children:"paper v2, Table 5(b)"})," reports EgoSchema-subset accuracy of 66.2, 64.4 and 61.2 for the full method, removal of depth expansion, and the further removal of adaptive breadth. This is video QA, dependent on caption fidelity, not game debugging."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Availability and terms."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Ziyang412/VideoTree",children:"Public repository"}),", MIT ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Ziyang412/VideoTree/blob/main/LICENSE",children:"license"}),"; Python 3.8+, GPU-oriented clustering/features and an LLM are documented. Dataset/model/provider terms remain separate. Training-free still uses pretrained models."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap adaptation, unimplemented."})," Treat the output as an index over retained raw evidence. Compare uniform sampling, fixed-width clustering, adaptive breadth only and breadth-plus-depth at equal total caption/model budgets. Include repeated states and brief transitions. Replacing final captions with pixels creates a new adapter."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"4-longvu-temporal-filtering-and-selective-spatial-token-retention",children:"4. LongVU: temporal filtering and selective spatial-token retention"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Mechanism and reported result."})," LongVU fuses DINOv2/SigLIP features, removes temporally redundant frames, gives query-relevant frames greater spatial-token resolution, then drops spatial tokens redundant across neighboring frames. In the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v267/shen25j.html",children:"ICML 2025 paper, Table 3"}),", the 8K-context VideoMME scores progress from 57.56 for uniform 64-token frames to 59.90 with DINO temporal reduction, 60.08 with query selection and 60.56 with spatial compression. Temporal reduction alone slightly lowers EgoSchema versus the 64-token uniform baseline, so the components are not universally beneficial."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Source-inspected contract."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Vision-CAIR/LongVU/blob/1b0be5cc28614b03a423bbaf129ae364750b5012/longvu/cambrian_arch.py",children:e.jsx(t.code,{children:"longvu/cambrian_arch.py"})})," exposes ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"select_frame(feature_list, split_sizes, input_ids, new_image_aux_list, image_sizes, window_size=16, threshold=0.83)"}),". It returns selected features, updated frame counts, two selected image tensors and original selection indices. Its long-video branch retains window-center anchors and caps selected frames at 400. Query-ranked resolution allocation and spatial-token dropping occur inside multimodal-input preparation, with additional truncation under pressure. These internal embeddings cannot shorten an unrelated hosted model’s visual context."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Vision-CAIR/LongVU/blob/main/README.md",children:"README inference path"})," decodes roughly one frame per second, preprocesses them, and calls ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"model.generate(input_ids, images=video, image_sizes=...)"}),". It emits answer text, not an evidence manifest; the documented local demo asks for a 40G GPU."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Availability and terms."})," Public code with Apache-2.0 ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/Vision-CAIR/LongVU/blob/main/LICENSE",children:"LICENSE"}),", Qwen2-7B and Llama3.2-3B checkpoints linked. Both inspected upstream checkpoint pages display Apache-2.0 metadata (",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/Vision-CAIR/LongVU_Qwen2_7B",children:"Qwen2"}),", ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/Vision-CAIR/LongVU_Llama3_2_3B",children:"Llama3.2"}),"); this does not replace review of the base-model and training-data terms."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap adaptation, unimplemented."})," Keep this as a model-internal research track, separate from pi harness-only optimization. Hold backbone/weights/evaluator fixed and ablate temporal reduction, resolution allocation and spatial dropping. Export provenance; measure rare-event recall, text loss and temporal-order errors. One FPS decoding cannot recover an event it never sampled."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"5-automated-bug-frame-retrieval-useful-retrieval-pipeline-unsafe-headline-metric",children:"5. Automated Bug Frame Retrieval: useful retrieval pipeline, unsafe headline metric"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Paper-described interface."})," Re-encode gameplay video to H.264 medium, extract encoding keyframes, summarize the bug report with a visual/nonvisual flag, and ask GPT-4o for JSON ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"Explanation"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"Ranking"})," (frame filenames), or no result. Consecutive batches are re-ranked in a second pass. Candidate coverage and final retrieval success must remain distinct."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Metric caution."})," ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"Accuracy@N=TP@N/(TP@N+FN)"})," excludes false positives, so 0.89 is not whole-video accuracy. The reported pass@3≈0.98 also fails its own arithmetic: ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"1-(1-.68)^3≈.967"}),", and independent identical trials are not established. The 94 never-correct videos would imply ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"256/350≈73.1%"})," with any correct outcome, including correct abstentions, but the repeat-run tallies are inconsistent: the 183/48/25 videos correct in 3/2/1 runs imply 670 correct outcomes, whereas Table 3 reports ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"528 TP@1+184 TN=712"}),". Treat 73.1% as an implication of one reported tally, not a verified empirical pass@3; do not cite 98% as a measured result. Industrial data came from one first-person-shooter game; no public executable/data release was identified in the paper. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.04895v1",children:"Paper v1, Table 3 and §5.3"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap adaptation, unimplemented."})," Keep separate denominators for candidate-frame coverage, correct retrieval among all bug-bearing videos, false-positive retrieval on clean videos, and correct abstention. Compare encoding keyframes, uniform and event-aware sampling on owned fixtures. Preserve original timestamp mappings. Return temporal neighborhoods for animation/stutter faults; single stills cannot establish them."]}),`
