`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Checked 2026-10-19. A released screenshot-to-region interface for editor UI and game HUD observation, with concrete label/coordinate hazards. It complements query-directed V*/SEAL search and temporal trackers; it does not establish game-creation, repair or gameplay gains. No model, engine, installation, weight download, API inference or fixture execution."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"source-boundary",children:"Source boundary"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Microsoft OmniParser source inspected at ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de"}),", the default-branch commit returned on the check date. This July 2026 revision changes the default detector to YOLOv9-E, so old YOLOv8-only descriptions do not describe this interface. The model repository's observed head was ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"f55d0750e5b94db2125ef0b45b0fa4a85ddc59b4"}),"; its ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/microsoft/OmniParser-v2.0/commit/f55d0750e5b94db2125ef0b45b0fa4a85ddc59b4",children:"merge diff"})," establishes that the new weight and MIT license were released. No weight bytes were downloaded or independently hashed. Direct pinned model-file pages failed to load; folder-license observations below use separately scoped rolling pages."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"released-inputoutput-surface",children:"Released input/output surface"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The local ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/omnitool/omniparserserver/omniparserserver.py#L16-L48",children:"FastAPI server"})," exposes POST ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"/parse/"})," with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"base64_image: str"}),"; it returns ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"som_image_base64"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"parsed_content_list"})," and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"latency"}),". GET ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"/probe/"})," is a readiness response. This is published self-hostable server source, not evidence of a maintained public inference endpoint or successful local execution. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/microsoft/OmniParser-v2.0",children:"model page"})," reported no Inference Provider deployment when checked."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/util/omniparser.py#L16-L32",children:"parser wrapper"})," decodes the image, runs EasyOCR and icon detection/captioning, and returns a numbered overlay plus element records. Records contain ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"type"})," (",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"text"}),"/",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"icon"}),"), normalized ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"bbox: [x1,y1,x2,y2]"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"interactivity"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"content"}),", and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"source"}),". The client later adds ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"idx"}),". OCR, detector and caption outputs are fused; those records are not DOM/accessibility elements, engine object IDs, or validated action targets."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Two incompatible box shapes coexist."})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/util/utils.py#L349-L372",children:"The helper"})," additionally returns ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"label_coordinates"})," as a string-ID dictionary of ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"(x,y,width,height)"}),", pixels by default and ratios when requested. In contrast, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"parsed_content_list[].bbox"})," remains normalized corner coordinates. The public parser wrapper discards the helper's coordinate dictionary. A consumer must name both coordinate space and box format; ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"output_coord_in_ratio"})," is not a general switch for every returned structure. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/util/utils.py#L416-L496",children:"Conversion and return path"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"resize-crop-and-original-image-mapping",children:"Resize, crop and original-image mapping"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The current ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/util/yolov9.py#L52-L87",children:"YOLOv9 adapter"})," rounds requested canvas dimensions up to multiples of 32, aspect-fits the screenshot, truncates resized dimensions to integers, and centers it on a ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"(114,114,114)"})," canvas. It restores detector boxes by subtracting left/top padding, dividing by the nominal scale and clamping to original image dimensions before returning pixel ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"xyxy"}),". ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/util/yolov9.py#L115-L136",children:"Inverse mapping"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The server wrapper sets ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"scale_img=False"}),"; consequently ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"predict_yolo"})," does not forward ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"imgsz"}),", and this adapter uses its default 640 canvas. The model card's separate example uses 1280, top-left padding, different resizing and suppression settings. Those are distinct configurations, not interchangeable recipes; neither establishes accuracy for tiny editor controls. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/util/utils.py#L390-L445",children:"Caller and detector dispatch"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The default Florence/non-Phi caption path crops selected icon regions from the original screenshot using integer pixel boundaries, then stretches them to 64×64 before processing. OCR-only regions are not all captioned, and the separate Phi path does not use this resize. This can remove surrounding UI context and alter aspect ratio. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/util/utils.py#L88-L131",children:"Caption crop path"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Any caller-supplied viewport crop or resize is outside those inverse transforms. Proposed GameMap mapping: normalized box → input screenshot pixels → inverse caller resize/padding → source-frame crop offset → desktop/window coordinates only if actions need them. Record original/crop dimensions, offsets, rounding, display scale and window position; a ratio does not encode these transforms. Keep image and action coordinate spaces separate."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"ids-interpretation-and-failure-boundaries",children:"IDs, interpretation and failure boundaries"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/omnitool/gradio/agent/llm_utils/omniparserclient.py#L14-L44",children:"client"})," enumerates records afresh, attaches screenshot width/height, original screenshot bytes and a filename UUID. There is no temporal matching in this path. IDs are valid for this parse/overlay only; sorting and overlap filtering can renumber them on a later frame. The server alone supplies neither frame ID nor image hash. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/omnitool/gradio/tools/screen_capture.py#L10-L27",children:"Screenshot UUID creation"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/omnitool/gradio/agent/vlm_agent.py#L149-L168",children:"action consumer"})," indexes the current record list by predicted Box ID and takes the normalized-box midpoint times screenshot dimensions. That is a coordinate proposal, not proof the target is enabled, unobscured or still present when clicked. A screenshot UUID is useful association metadata but does not establish freshness or pixel identity."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.code,{children:"interactivity"})," is assigned false to OCR text and true to detector icons in the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/util/utils.py#L251-L328",children:"fusion path"}),", not checked against application state. Overlapping OCR may become icon content; an icon inside OCR may be removed. Its overlap criterion includes intersection/individual-area ratios as well as IoU. Returned source labels distinguish OCR/fused/caption paths, but detector confidence is not preserved in these element records. Icon descriptions are generated interpretations, not verified semantics."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Source-visible edge case, unexecuted:"})," when no OCR boxes are found, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"get_som_labeled_img"})," sets ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ocr_bbox=None"})," then immediately evaluates ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"zip(ocr_bbox, ocr_text)"}),". This is an unguarded failure path in the inspected code, especially relevant to text-free viewports; do not report it as a reproduced crash or convert a parser failure into “no objects.” ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/util/utils.py#L437-L446",children:"Exact branch"})]}),`
`]}),`
