`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The pinned repository's ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/LICENSE",children:"LICENSE"})," is ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"CC-BY-4.0"}),", despite the ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/README.md",children:"README"})," MIT badge. Preserve that discrepancy. The model folders separately declare ",e.jsxs(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/microsoft/OmniParser-v2.0/blob/main/icon_detect_v3/LICENSE",children:["YOLOv9-E ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"icon_detect_v3"}),": MIT"]}),", ",e.jsxs(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/microsoft/OmniParser-v2.0/blob/main/icon_caption/LICENSE",children:["Florence ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"icon_caption"}),": MIT"]}),", and ",e.jsxs(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/microsoft/OmniParser-v2.0/blob/main/icon_detect/LICENSE",children:["legacy ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"icon_detect"}),": AGPL-3.0"]}),". The model card's permissive-pipeline language does not resolve the repository license mismatch or dependency terms. The source ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser/blob/354021201345a96178360b28733573e27269f2de/requirements.txt",children:"requirements"})," still include Ultralytics. The detector loader can fetch rolling ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"main"}),"; pin source, actual weight/config and OCR/caption dependencies independently before any future use."]}),`
