`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Compare global screenshot; screenshot plus OCR regions; screenshot plus full OmniParser records/overlay. Hold screenshots, model, task set, permissions and total observation budget fixed; include preprocessing/caption latency and failures. Use owned editor/HUD fixtures with repeated icons, tiny controls, nested text/buttons, disabled controls, a viewport crop and a moved window; include blank/text-free inputs and a stale parse after a layout change."}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Score region recall, text/semantic correctness, coordinate round-trip error and target selection separately; then measure an authorized action's actual result if needed. Reject stale ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"(frame hash, parse ID, region index)"})," references, retain original evidence and authoritative UI/engine assertions, and treat missing/failed parses as explicit outcomes. This tests a GUI observation adapter, not general game understanding or engine-state truth."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"7-fiftyone-persistent-retrieval-over-capture-evidence",children:"7. FiftyOne: persistent retrieval over capture evidence"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Checked ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"2026-10-19"}),". This fills a distinct gap beside V*/SEAL, VideoTree, LongVU, VideoAgent and OmniParser: a released dataset/view/index interface for revisiting stored frames and failed regions across edit iterations. It is not a visual reasoning model or evidence of improved game creation. Source inspection only; no installation, server, model, embedding, media download or execution."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Source boundary."})," FiftyOne inspected at ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"aacfc8182fc5353296b5edd7475e63335fedb5cb"}),"; its separate Brain repository at ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ba978a12293fda9953b478f601ac8950d2a35aa4"}),". These independently resolved revisions identify the inspected contracts, not a tested compatible installation."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{id:"identity-coordinates-and-mutation-boundaries",children:"Identity, coordinates and mutation boundaries"}),`
