`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Source scope:"})," ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://arxiv.org/html/2604.07818v2",children:"paper v2"}),", plus six inspected files at upstream commit ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"0626688f2b2eab5414d8f8e28e682cfaf607c0ab"})," (2026-10-18). This is offline gameplay-video diagnosis, not a game-creation agent or authoritative physics assertion."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Interface and mechanism:"})," The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/SandyyyZheng/GliDe/blob/0626688f2b2eab5414d8f8e28e682cfaf607c0ab/README.md",children:"README"})," documents video/game-name inputs, frame-window screening, targeted VQA/crops and optional SAM3 tracking, then event grouping and interval refinement. Output JSON contains bug descriptions and one or more second-based intervals per bug. Optional tracking can be disabled when unavailable, so tool availability must accompany a result. Intermediate artifacts can be saved."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Actual information policy:"})," In ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/SandyyyZheng/GliDe/blob/0626688f2b2eab5414d8f8e28e682cfaf607c0ab/graph.py",children:"graph.py"}),", game context is the longest of the first three distinct nonempty scanner descriptions. It is inferred context, not a retrieved authoritative rulebook. No positive scanner window routes directly to summarization, skipping detailed analysis and grounding. ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/SandyyyZheng/GliDe/blob/0626688f2b2eab5414d8f8e28e682cfaf607c0ab/analyzer/memory.py",children:"Memory code"})," compresses older debate rounds in planner context to judge conclusions; the latest two get more detail. Serialized tool evidence supplied to debate prompts is truncated to a 1,500-character prefix, followed by an omission notice. Full stored evidence and model-visible evidence therefore differ."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Reported evidence:"})," The paper's Qwen2.5-VL-7B ablation reports description F1 of 39.12 with the full system, 33.03 without game context and 32.17 without debate; grounding removal changes its mIoU from 0.53 to 0.32. Those are the authors' dataset/backbone-specific findings, not a matched-cost claim or proof of reliable project QA. A single unusual pose can be valid game behavior; disconnected temporal intervals can describe one recurring event."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Evaluator discrepancy and denominators:"})," The paper assigns pairs using semantic score multiplied by temporal IoU; the pinned ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/SandyyyZheng/GliDe/blob/0626688f2b2eab5414d8f8e28e682cfaf607c0ab/evaluation/evaluator.py",children:"evaluator.py"})," assigns using semantic score alone, then computes overlap. Its description precision/recall sum matched 0–5 judge scores and divide by ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"5 × predicted/ground-truth bug count"}),"; this is soft description credit, not thresholded true-positive counting. The paper's printed equations omit that factor of five. Mean IoU averages matched pairs only; unmatched events do not enter that mean, and correct no-bug videos do not increase the description numerator. The dataset loop uses only shared ground-truth/prediction names, so missing predictions are excluded. Description-scoring errors can become zero scores. Matching, normalization, missing-output policy and judge failures must be reconciled before calling a run a paper reproduction."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Release and terms:"})," Pipeline and evaluator files are public; ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://github.com/SandyyyZheng/GliDe/blob/0626688f2b2eab5414d8f8e28e682cfaf607c0ab/LICENSE",children:"code license"})," is MIT. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/datasets/SandyZheng33/VideoGlitchBench",children:"dataset card"})," declares Apache-2.0, 4,717 glitch clips and 521 negative clips, with annotations and game-organized video files. Its viewer's split label is ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"train"}),"; that does not establish a held-out optimization protocol. Underlying game/video rights and model dependencies still need separate review. No data archive, model or service was run."]}),`
`]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Comparison template:"})," compare uniform-window screening, game-context only, debate only and temporal grouping under both equal call/token budgets and reported wall time. Measure candidate-window recall before downstream analysis; include rare brief failures and legitimate stylized movement. Freeze a complete expected-episode manifest, count absent/error outputs separately, preserve report-to-frame references and state whether matching follows paper or code. Compare compressed judge summaries against raw evidence under the same context budget; keep authoritative project rules separate from model-inferred memory. None of these ablations is implemented here."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"visual-qa-tasks-as-observation-checks-videogameqa-bench",children:"Visual QA tasks as observation checks: VideoGameQA-Bench"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://asgaardlab.github.io/videogameqa-bench/",children:"official project"})," separates scene/UI questions, acceptable-versus-unacceptable screenshot changes, parametric clipping, glitch detection, bug descriptions and first-glitch localization. This supplies concrete observation tests: an image pair plus change policy yields a regression judgment; a scene image plus typed questions yields structured attributes; a video yields detection and a first-occurrence answer. These outputs do not establish gameplay-state or collision correctness. The authors report particular difficulty with fine scene/UI details and temporal localization."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://asgaardlab.github.io/videogameqa-bench/artifacts.html",children:"artifact page"})," exposes per-model results, error counts and differing evaluated sample totals. The ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"https://huggingface.co/datasets/taesiri/VideoGameQA-Bench",children:"public dataset card"})," declares CC-BY-4.0. Those are available evaluation materials; a complete runnable evaluator was not established in this inspection. Retain the exact task version, answer schema, timestamp units, error denominator and source-media rights before reuse."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Use original project-owned controlled scenes to test whether crops, image pairs or temporal packets actually preserve a small prop, HUD value, contact transition or brief anomaly. Score evidence selection separately from the final diagnosis and from the agent's repair. A better-written bug report alone is not a more accurate detector."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"asset-feedback-and-candidate-choice",children:"Asset feedback and candidate choice"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["See ",e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/asset-selection-feedback/",children:"Asset selection and visual-feedback creation"})," for SceneSmith, Reward3D, MuMA, SceneAssistant and AVR-Agent: first-acceptable versus ranked selection, multi-view scoring, actual model-visible evidence and counterevidence to universal refinement gains."]}),`
