`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Observation packet."})," Retain original video/images and build ID; record source timestamps or simulation ticks, camera/viewport, crop-to-original mapping, selection query, model-derived masks/labels, selected and rejected candidate IDs, and omitted-frame ranges. A compact packet should point back to original evidence rather than replacing it."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Matched baselines."})," Compare uniform time samples, event-triggered samples and query-adaptive samples at equal frame/pixel budgets; compare full frames versus crop-plus-global-context at equal visual-token budgets. Report selector calls, preprocessing, generation attempts, latency and failures as well as final-model tokens. For learned compression, report the changed checkpoint/architecture separately from prompt/tool-only harness changes."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Useful counterexamples."})," Include brief contact failures, valid exaggerated animation, occluded objects, repeated events separated by normal intervals, small HUD changes and empty/missing captures. For assets, test back views, scale/axis/pivot, alpha/material behavior and target-engine import in a future authorized fixture; an aesthetically preferred thumbnail cannot certify these properties."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Separate outcomes."})," Score evidence coverage, temporal/spatial localization, diagnosis, proposed repair, executed functional result and subjective quality independently. Keep a no-feedback baseline and a same-budget extra-generation baseline; otherwise a feedback benefit may simply reflect additional attempts."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Prevent selection leakage."})," Use project/game-disjoint development and final sets where feasible. Freeze judge prompts and expected episode IDs before comparison. Do not expose held-out answer keys, final scores or inferred final-test lessons to persistent candidate memory. Account for failures, unavailable tools and abstentions rather than dropping them."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Pin and audit."})," Preserve source and model revisions, service names, raw tool results, compressed context and exact score implementation. Paper/code discrepancies need an explicit protocol choice before execution. Purpose-specific code, weight, data and service permissions remain a separate gate."]}),`
`]}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Remaining boundary:"})," the collection supports a bounded experiment design, but cannot select a universally best visual harness. That requires a chosen target game/project family, an authorized runtime, owned or cleared assets, calibrated acceptance assertions and a compute/latency budget. No such experiment is claimed here."]}),`
